[site-manifest
  [doc [#
docs-src/site/manifest.cxd — what cxhome.org serves (RULED: RS-28, D57a, D58a, D51d).

Read by scripts/gen_site/site_build.cx (`make site-index`, and `make docs` /
`make docs-check`: renders docs/index.html from [page]) and by
scripts/gen_site/site_assemble.cx (`make site`, `make site-check`); its [suites]
also by scripts/gen_guide/guide_build.cx (`make guide`). Declares:

  [site]    the site's own repository (the front door, `repo=`), the published
            base URL, and the output directory `make site` assembles
  [page]    the landing page: its Markdown source and the tracked, generated
            HTML it renders to
  [suites]  the conformance suites the landing page may cite with
            {{EXAMPLE:<id> …}} and a guide page with [fixture id=<id>] (the
            guide build replays each, RULED: RS-30), spelled as
            docs-src/llm/manifest.cxd spells
            them (a pinned suite as deps/<repo>/conformance/…)
  [files]   THE SITE: every file the assembled output directory holds, one
            path per line, relative to the site root, grouped by where it comes
            from. `make site-check` lists the assembled tree against the union
            of these blocks: a file missing from the tree, or present in it and
            claimed by no line, fails the step by name. A block may carry
            `optional=true`: its lines may be absent from the tree without
            failing MISSING, but a file present that no line — required or
            optional — declares still fails EXTRA. `required-when=VAR` makes
            an optional block REQUIRED whenever the environment variable VAR
            is "1" (the wasm bundle below, PLAY-1).

Where each group comes from is the map scripts/publish.sh applied before it
retired with the allowlist mirror (RULED: RS-11), now `make site`'s:
docs/guide/'s contents at the root, except the guide's own index.html, which
becomes guide.html (the root's index.html is the landing page); docs/llm/ under
llm/, with llms.txt and llms-full.txt copied to the root as well (D51d: the
assembly step copies them, untracked); the dev/ door (dev/index.html); docs/install and
docs/CNAME at the root; an empty .nojekyll.

Adding a guide section, a stdlib module (its reference page is lib-<name>.html)
or a docs/llm/ output adds its line here in the same change. A module renders
x-<name>.html only while its source glob-matches this front door's OWN
top-level x/*.cx (guide_build.cx's `is-x-file`, D63a: a PINNED repo's
deps/<repo>/x/*.cx never counts, however its source path reads) — with no
live x/ tier here today, no x-<name>.html line belongs in this manifest, and
`clean-stale-pages` (#1672, guide_build.cx) is what keeps one from
reappearing on its own: it sweeps every docs/guide/*.html a run does not
(re)write, so a module that moves tier, is renamed, or is retired never
leaves its old page for `site-check` to have to either reject or be told to
bless. #1672 is what this file's own history got wrong before this line was
written — see the `[files from=guide]` block's own note below.

The playground's wasm/ bundle is REQUIRED WHERE IT IS BUILT (PLAY-1):
`optional=true required-when=CX_SITE_REQUIRE_WASM`. The Site workflow builds
the engine with a pinned, cached emsdk (`make guide-wasm`) and sets
CX_SITE_REQUIRE_WASM=1, so the site cxhome.org serves fails `site-check`
MISSING without any one of the five files — the Site run 36375144472 shipped
0 of them while this block was plainly optional, and the page answered 404
for its engine. Everywhere else (the post-merge doc pipeline on a box with no
emcc, `make docs`) the same five lines are declared and optional: absent is
fine, and a wasm file no line declares still fails EXTRA.
#]]

  [site repo=cx base='https://cxhome.org/' out=site]

  [page src='docs-src/site/index.md' out='docs/index.html'
        title='CX — one language for your data and your code']

  [suites [#
