  [; the rendered guide (make guide, docs/guide/), at the root; the lib- pages
     are projected from the [module-doc]/[fn-doc] blocks of the pinned
     repositories' stdlib/*.cx and x/*.cx (82 bundled modules: the eleven the x/
     tier graduated keep the x/ SOURCE path in cx-platform-agent and
     cx-platform-ux, RULED: D45a, D63a — but graduated means graduated: they
     render as lib-<name>.html same as any frozen module, because is-x-file
     reads only this front door's own top-level x/*.cx, never a pinned repo's),
     the codec- pages from the synthesized codecs.
     #1672: this list once carried 12 x-<name>.html lines that no build of the
     tree this HEAD produces can generate — orphans from before D45a/D63a
     graduated the last cohort and/or before the repo split moved their
     sources under deps/, when the front door's OWN x/ still existed and
     `make guide` never cleans a page whose source moved out from under it.
     One long-lived checkout still carried them on disk (a fresh `make guide`
     here never does; measured on this branch's own worktree, zero x- pages,
     same 82 modules, all lib-). guide_build.cx's `clean-stale-pages` closes
     the actual gap: it sweeps every docs/guide/*.html a run does not
     (re)write, so the next tier move or rename cannot leave a page behind
     for this list to have to either reject or bless. ]
